2. Flatten Nested Logic with any() and all()Avoid messy chains of if / elif / or conditions when validating business rules or configurations. 

Use any() and all() paired with generator expressions for instant readability.

flags = [True, False, True]
user_inputs = ["admin", "password123", ""]

# Check if at least one flag is active
if any(flags):
    print("Action required.")

# Ensure all strings in a list are non-empty
if all(len(item) > 0 for item in user_inputs):
    print("All inputs are valid.")



